### Public booking API (spec §6.1) — manual scenario
# Works with the REST Client (VS Code) / JetBrains HTTP Client.
# 1. `docker compose up mongo`, `pnpm seed`, `pnpm dev`.
# 2. Run "config", copy ids into the variables below (location, barber, service, extra).
# 3. Run "days" → "slots" → "quote" → "create". The cancel token is in the confirmation email
#    (without RESEND_API_KEY it is printed to the server console) — put it into @token.
#
# Errors: `{ "error": { "code": "SLOT_TAKEN", "details": { ... } } }`, the HTTP status matches the type.
# Codes: VALIDATION_ERROR (details.fields), PHONE_INVALID, RATE_LIMITED (429, Retry-After),
# BOOKING_REJECTED (honeypot), BOOKING_DISABLED, LOCATION_NOT_FOUND, BARBER_NOT_FOUND,
# SERVICE_NOT_FOUND, EXTRA_NOT_FOUND, EXTRA_NOT_APPLICABLE, SLOT_TAKEN, SLOT_UNAVAILABLE,
# PROMO_NOT_FOUND, PROMO_EXPIRED, PROMO_LIMIT, PROMO_CLIENT_LIMIT, PROMO_NOT_APPLICABLE,
# CERTIFICATE_NOT_FOUND, ACTIVE_BOOKINGS_LIMIT, TOKEN_INVALID, CANCEL_NOT_ALLOWED, CANCEL_TOO_LATE.
# Money — integer bani (MDL × 100); instants — ISO UTC; dates — local `YYYY-MM-DD` (Europe/Chisinau).
# Limits: reads 30/min per IP; bookings 5 created/h and 20 attempts/h per IP, 10 attempts/h per phone,
# 3 active future bookings per phone.

@api = http://localhost:3000/api
@location = 000000000000000000000000
@barber = 000000000000000000000000
@service = 000000000000000000000000
@extra = 000000000000000000000000
@date = 2026-12-01
@token = paste-the-token-from-the-email

### Config: locations, barbers (online), categories, services ("from" prices), extras, settings
GET {{api}}/booking/config?locale=ro

### Days with free slots (barber = id or `any`; range clamped to today … today + horizon, ≤ 62 days)
GET {{api}}/booking/days?location={{location}}&barber=any&service={{service}}&extras[]={{extra}}&from={{date}}&to=2026-12-31

### Slots of a day; `barbers` — who is free, the auto-pick first
GET {{api}}/booking/slots?location={{location}}&barber={{barber}}&service={{service}}&extras[]={{extra}}&date={{date}}

### Quote for a barber (without `barber` / `any` → cheapest of the possible barbers, `priceFrom: true`)
POST {{api}}/booking/quote
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "location": "{{location}}",
  "barber": "{{barber}}",
  "service": "{{service}}",
  "extras": ["{{extra}}"],
  "promoCode": "LEVELUP10",
  "certificateCode": null
}

### Create (new or known phone — the response is the same; known client data are not changed)
POST {{api}}/booking
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "location": "{{location}}",
  "barber": "any",
  "service": "{{service}}",
  "extras": [],
  "start": "2026-12-01T08:00:00.000Z",
  "phone": "069 123 456",
  "firstName": "Ion",
  "lastName": "Popescu",
  "email": "delivered@resend.dev",
  "language": "ro",
  "promoCode": null,
  "certificateCode": null,
  "comment": "Prima vizită",
  "honeypot": ""
}

### Honeypot filled → 400 BOOKING_REJECTED
POST {{api}}/booking
Content-Type: application/json

{ "honeypot": "http://spam.example" }

### Invalid phone → 400 PHONE_INVALID
POST {{api}}/booking
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "location": "{{location}}",
  "service": "{{service}}",
  "start": "2026-12-01T08:00:00.000Z",
  "phone": "123",
  "firstName": "Ion",
  "language": "ru"
}

### Cancel: details and `canCancel` (scheduled and ≥ clientCancelMinHours before the start)
GET {{api}}/booking/cancel/{{token}}?locale=ro

### Cancel (→ cancelled_by_client; too late → CANCEL_TOO_LATE, already cancelled → CANCEL_NOT_ALLOWED)
POST {{api}}/booking/cancel/{{token}}
